{#
	The control plane's own header (XIV-101).

	**This is the "second page" XIV-58 said to wait for.** That page's template
	said, in as many words, that its header was small because there was one page
	to navigate between and that a nav belonged to the moment there was a second.
	This is that moment, so the header moved out of `tenants.html.twig` into a
	partial rather than being copied into `modules.html.twig` — two headers with
	one sign-out link between them is how a sign-out link ends up on one page and
	not the other.

	**Still not `_topbar.html.twig`.** That bar is the tenant application's
	navigation — a customer's modules, their company name, their account menu —
	and every one of those needs a resolved tenant, which this host deliberately
	has not got (§8.9). Two links and a sign-out is the whole of what an operator
	can navigate to, and it is drawn here rather than borrowed.

	`current` is the route name of the page including this, so the active item can
	be marked without the partial guessing from `app.request`.
#}
<div class="d-flex align-items-center justify-content-between mb-4">
	<div class="d-flex align-items-baseline gap-3">
		<h1 class="h4 mb-0">{{ 'control_plane.title'|trans }}</h1>
		{#
			`aria-current` as well as the colour, because "which page am I on" is
			exactly the question a colour alone answers only for people who can see
			it. Same rule the status badges on the tenant list follow.
		#}
		<nav class="nav nav-pills small" aria-label="{{ 'control_plane.title'|trans }}">
			<a class="nav-link py-1 {{ current == 'control_plane_home' ? 'active' : '' }}"
			   {{ current == 'control_plane_home' ? 'aria-current="page"' : '' }}
			   href="{{ path('control_plane_home') }}">{{ 'control_plane.tenants'|trans }}</a>
			<a class="nav-link py-1 {{ current == 'control_plane_modules' ? 'active' : '' }}"
			   {{ current == 'control_plane_modules' ? 'aria-current="page"' : '' }}
			   href="{{ path('control_plane_modules') }}">{{ 'control_plane.modules'|trans }}</a>
		</nav>
	</div>
	<div class="d-flex align-items-center gap-3">
		<span class="text-body-secondary small">{{ app.user.name }}</span>
		<a class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary" href="{{ path('control_plane_logout') }}">
			{{ 'nav.sign_out'|trans }}
		</a>
	</div>
</div>
